// Liveness: a whole-program stall must be REPORTED, not sat on. A bare recv
// on a channel nobody sends to used to hang silently on both backends
// (analysis experiment deadlock2, exit 124 by timeout); the runtime now
// proves quiescence (no ready work, timers, I/O waiters, async jobs, or
// sys.Thread) with channel waiters parked, prints the fatal report, and
// exits 71 (task 260 §4).
//
// vm_only: the v1 detector activates only on cores with a VM owner — the
// AOT thread-spawn path keeps no census the neutral scheduler can read, so
// an AOT-standalone core cannot prove "no live threads" and stays silent
// (documented deviation; the AOT leg follows with a neutral census).
print("before recv")
var ch = Channel<i64>(0)
var got = match (ch.recv()) {
    Recv.Value(v) -> v
    _ -> -1
}
print(got)
